<item>
            <title>[JGVT-4355] Reports_Audit Trail: Audit Trails- export_must be reliable</title>
                <link>https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-4355</link>
                <project id="46901" key="JGVT">TDS - Revvity Signals ELN</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;As a&lt;/b&gt; user,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;I want to&lt;/b&gt; be able to export the experiment history to an Excel or PDF file and be 100% of the correctness and reliability of the export,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;so that&lt;/b&gt; I can trust the information with an audit.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;Design notes&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;during UAT testing on &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-2248&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: Experiment Audit Trail- Excel export_must have&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-2248&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-2248&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; , a time-out occurred when retrieving data for the attributes sheet. The time-out setting has to be extended, to prevent that this will happen again in the future. This has to be checked for all data retrievals, because time-out can occur every time.&#160;&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;If an error happens, the user has to be informed that an empty excel sheet is caused by an error and not because no data were found.&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;DEV notes&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;increase the time-out setting. Q: Is this a configurable value, or does this require a code change?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;show the error message in a readable way on the excel sheet for which the error occurred, including a timestamp when it occured&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This applies for Experiment and System audit trail (which means for the Excel and PDF export)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;TEST notes&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We need to find a way to trigger an error, to make this story testable. &lt;br/&gt;
e.g. set the timeout to a very low value during testing and check if the error message shows up, and afterwards set the timeout back to the normal value and check if the system works normal&lt;/p&gt;</description>
